  "raw_response": "Root cause is `_extract_tar_dir()` indexing `tar._ansible_normalized_cache` instead of `TarFile.getmember()`, with the cache populated by stripping trailing separators.\n\nRelevant files:\n- [sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0:lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py?L1559-L1577](/r/github.com/sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0/-/blob/lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py?L1559-L1577) - Builds the private normalized tar-member cache.\n- [sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0:lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py?L1590-L1603](/r/github.com/sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0/-/blob/lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py?L1590-L1603) - Reads `FILES.json` and dispatches directory entries to `_extract_tar_dir()`.\n- [sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0:lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py?L1657-L1685](/r/github.com/sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0/-/blob/lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py?L1657-L1685) - Fragile directory lookup and extraction implementation.\n- [sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0:test/units/cli/galaxy/test_collection_extract_tar.py?L14-L50](/r/github.com/sg-evals/ansible--v2.16.0/-/blob/test/units/cli/galaxy/test_collection_extract_tar.py?L14-L50) - Existing unit coverage for the private cache behavior.",
